      {
        "id": "thm-neutral-delay-euler-first-order-error",
        "kind": "theorem",
        "title": "Compatible-grid Euler has first-order solution and derivative error for a stable neutral delay",
        "deps": [
          "def-scalar-neutral-delay-equation-and-segment-shift",
          "thm-neutral-delay-method-of-steps-well-posedness",
          "lem-neutral-delay-shift-neumann-inverse",
          "alg-neutral-delay-euler-compatible-grid",
          "lem-discrete-one-step-error-recurrence-bound",
          "cor-vector-valued-ftc-and-lipschitz-bound",
          "thm-norm-inequality-for-the-vector-valued-integral",
          "thm-cauchy-schwarz-and-the-euclidean-norm",
          "def-vector-valued-functions-limits-and-continuity"
        ],
        "justified_by": [],
        "dependency_level": 3,
        "statement": "Let $T=K\\tau$ with integers $K,m\\ge1$, set $h=\\tau/m$ and $N=Km$, and let\n$|a|<1$. Assume the compatible scalar neutral-delay problem of\n[[def-scalar-neutral-delay-equation-and-segment-shift]] has the unique solution\n$y$ supplied by [[thm-neutral-delay-method-of-steps-well-posedness]]. Suppose\n$y$ is $C^1$ on $[0,T]$, each grid-cell restriction is $C^2$ with one-sided\nendpoint derivatives, and $|y''(t)|\\le M$ on each cell interior for a constant\n$M\\ge0$. Apply [[alg-neutral-delay-euler-compatible-grid]] with exact history\nvalues and complete all $N$ updates (no budget or an integer budget $B\\ge N$).\nPut $\\Lambda=2L/(1-|a|)$. If $\\Lambda>0$, set\n$C_T=(M/2)(e^{\\Lambda T}-1)/\\Lambda$; if $\\Lambda=0$, set $C_T=MT/2$.\nThen\n$$\\max_{0\\le n\\le N}|Y_n-y(t_n)|\\le C_T h,\\qquad\\max_{0\\le n<N}|V_n-y'(t_n)|\\le\\Lambda C_T h.$$\n\n"
      },
